    "nemotron_h": {
      "uses": [
        "core",
        "loaders",
        "quant",
        "mamba2"
      ],
      "own": [
        "decoder/forward_nemotron.go"
      ],
      "deps_hash": "sha256:eb127d1bf747aa807dd4414ae42113fd5769f7b80ed75a45930f517f1ef65aa7",
      "status": "validated",
      "validated_at": "c3e43c8",
      "date": "2026-08-15",
      "reference": "HF bf16 \u2014 dense NVIDIA-Nemotron-Nano-9B-v2 (int8 resident) AND MoE NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-30B-A3B (int8 weights, f32 activations)",
      "machine": "linux-62gb",
      "method": "real-model-oracle",
      "metrics": {
        "argmax_pct": 100.0,
        "cosine_min": 0.99574,
        "cosine_mean": 0.99574,
        "moe_cosine_min": 0.997668,
        "moe_argmax_pct": 100.0,
        "moe_continuation_exact": true
      },
      "note": "Two real-checkpoint oracles back this family, because nemotron_h covers two architectures under one model_type: the DENSE 9B (cosine 0.99574, int8int8) and the MoE 30B-A3B Nemotron 3 Nano (cosine 0.997668, continuation exact). One row and not a sibling because the manifest is keyed by REGISTRY model_type and the registry dispatches both on nemotron_h -- unlike deepseek_v2/deepseek_v3, which are genuinely separate keys.\nThe MoE oracle runs at int8 WEIGHTS with f32 ACTIVATIONS, and that is a measured requirement, not a threshold dodge: int8int8 gives 0.978086 on the same forward. This model routes 6 of 128 experts (4.7%), far sparser than deepseek_v3 (0.99951), qwen3_5_moe (0.99333) or granitemoehybrid (0.99566) -- all at int8int8 -- and its own dense parent scores 0.99574 at int8int8. Quantizing activations perturbs the router enough to flip which experts run, a discrete change no averaging smooths. DEPLOYMENT FACT: do not run the MoE variant with int8 activations."
    },
